From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: count the game's XInput state reads for the host app

The host app offers a Keyboard & mouse on-screen layout to a game on
the Gamepad layout that has not asked for an XInput state within 20 s
of play after its first frame (Playport's touch-controls plan, phase
4: the suggested starting layout). Only win32u sees those requests:
the app's own reads of the controller snapshot go to
winios_gamepad_get_state directly, so a count there would include
them.

ios_gamepad_query now calls the host's playport_gamepad_state_read
(HostIO hio_pads.c) for each state request (op 0), whatever the slot,
before the empty-slot return; capability requests are not counted. The
reference is weak: a host that does not define it is not called.

Linear: PLA-533
Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/plans/2026-10-09-touch-controls.md (phase 4 item 3; host test app/tests/pads_test.c; phone gate not run)
Offered-upstream: no; the count feeds the iOS app's suggested layout
---
 build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c b/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c
index 25bee8f..cbb42af 100644
--- a/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c
+++ b/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c
@@ -2599,6 +2599,11 @@ C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct ios_xinput_state) == 16 );
 C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct ios_xinput_caps) == 20 );
 C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct winios_gamepad) == 20 );
 
+/* Playport: the host app counts the game's XInput state reads (its
+ * HostIO hio_pads.c), to tell a game that never asks for a pad. Weak: a
+ * host without it is not called. */
+extern void playport_gamepad_state_read( void ) __attribute__((weak));
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           ios_gamepad_query
  *
@@ -2614,6 +2619,11 @@ ULONG_PTR ios_gamepad_query( UINT index, UINT op, void *buffer )
     struct winios_gamepad pad;
 
     if (!buffer || index >= 4) return 0;
+    /* Every state request counts (XInputGetState; xinput's SetState and
+     * Enable ask for one too), for a slot with no pad as well: most games ask
+     * all four users each frame. The app's own snapshot reads do not come
+     * here. */
+    if (op == 0 && playport_gamepad_state_read) playport_gamepad_state_read();
     if (!winios_gamepad_get_state( index, &pad )) return 0;
 
     switch (op)
